    "title": "New Hartford detectives complete advanced homicide training",
    "text": "21 hours ago New Hartford Police Sergeant W.J. Freiberger and Investigator Annemarie Brelinsky from the Criminal Investigation Division completed the New York State Police Bureau of Criminal Investigation’s 38th Annual Colonel Henry F. Williams Homicide Investigation training in Albany during a recent five-day session. The seminar covered cold cases, forensic genetic genealogy, DNA technology, digital and video evidence, device-location evidence, and reviews of major homicide cases, giving local investigators new tools and contacts for complex investigations in the community. The New Hartford Police Department credits support and funding from the Oneida County District Attorney’s Office and First Source Federal Credit Union for helping make this training possible.\nThis content is adapted from materials provided by New Hartford Police Department\nThis article includes content summarized and organized with AI tools, which can make mistakes. Learn more.",
